235
01:08:17,333 --> 01:08:19,566
<b>Guatemala was permitted to intervene but</b>

236
01:08:19,566 --> 01:08:21,033
<b>strictly as a non-party</b>

237
01:08:21,266 --> 01:08:23,166
<b>and only on the question of sovereignty.</b>

238
01:08:24,133 --> 01:08:26,966
<b>Under ICJ rules, a decision only binds</b>

239
01:08:26,966 --> 01:08:28,066
<b>the parties to the case.</b>

240
01:08:28,966 --> 01:08:31,266
<b>Guatemala is in the room so the court can</b>

241
01:08:31,266 --> 01:08:33,033
<b>proceed without ignoring their rights.</b>

242
01:08:33,933 --> 01:08:34,666
<b>But Honduras isn't</b>

243
01:08:34,666 --> 01:08:36,300
<b>officially litigating against them.</b>

244
01:08:37,366 --> 01:08:38,266
<b>Consent preserved.</b>

245
01:08:38,899 --> 01:08:40,133
<b>The court's own words.</b>

246
01:08:40,933 --> 01:08:41,866
<b>Guatemala's interest</b>

247
01:08:41,866 --> 01:08:43,600
<b>is real and concrete.</b>

248
01:08:44,366 --> 01:08:46,566
<b>So why would Guatemala spend years and</b>

249
01:08:46,566 --> 01:08:48,800
<b>millions in legal fees fighting to sit</b>

250
01:08:48,800 --> 01:08:49,833
<b>in a courtroom where the</b>

251
01:08:49,833 --> 01:08:51,133
<b>ruling won't even bind them?</b>

252
01:08:51,366 --> 01:08:53,166
<b>They're there to stop the court from</b>

253
01:08:53,166 --> 01:08:55,266
<b>building a legal record they can't undo.</b>

254
01:08:55,966 --> 01:08:58,166
<b>Without Guatemala in the room, Belize</b>

255
01:08:58,166 --> 01:08:59,333
<b>presents its evidence.</b>

256
01:08:59,899 --> 01:09:01,733
<b>And if no one challenges it, the court</b>

257
01:09:01,733 --> 01:09:03,533
<b>accepts it as undisputed fact.</b>

258
01:09:04,233 --> 01:09:07,333
<b>A 200-page ICJ judgment explaining why</b>

259
01:09:07,333 --> 01:09:08,300
<b>Belize's history of</b>

260
01:09:08,300 --> 01:09:10,466
<b>possession is legally flawless</b>

261
01:09:10,733 --> 01:09:11,600
<b>creates a wall</b>

262
01:09:11,600 --> 01:09:14,066
<b>Guatemala can't climb in 2027.</b>

263
01:09:14,766 --> 01:09:17,566
<b>As a non-party, Guatemala can now submit</b>

264
01:09:17,566 --> 01:09:19,566
<b>written observations and challenge</b>

265
01:09:19,566 --> 01:09:20,899
<b>evidence in real time.</b>

266
01:09:21,166 --> 01:09:22,233
<b>They can introduce alternative</b>

267
01:09:22,233 --> 01:09:24,600
<b>interpretations of the 1859 Treaty</b>

268
01:09:24,866 --> 01:09:25,833
<b>before the court</b>

269
01:09:25,833 --> 01:09:27,133
<b>locks in Belize's version.</b>

270
01:09:27,666 --> 01:09:28,833
<b>Guatemala's main argument</b>

271
01:09:28,833 --> 01:09:30,566
<b>is "Uti Possidetis Juris".</b>

272
01:09:31,300 --> 01:09:31,966
<b>Colonial borders</b>

273
01:09:31,966 --> 01:09:33,233
<b>inherited that independence.</b>

274
01:09:34,533 --> 01:09:36,866
<b>Guatemala says it inherited sovereignty</b>

275
01:09:36,866 --> 01:09:38,800
<b>over these islands from Spain.</b>

276
01:09:39,466 --> 01:09:42,566
<b>The 1859 Treaty either didn't cover them</b>

277
01:09:42,566 --> 01:09:44,066
<b>or its void because</b>

278
01:09:44,066 --> 01:09:45,466
<b>Britain broke Article 7.</b>

279
01:09:46,133 --> 01:09:47,199
<b>Either way, the</b>

280
01:09:47,199 --> 01:09:48,600
<b>territory refers to Guatemala.</b>

281
01:09:49,733 --> 01:09:52,633
<b>After that, Belize has the 1913 letter,</b>

282
01:09:53,033 --> 01:09:54,366
<b>the 200 years of administration,</b>

283
01:09:55,166 --> 01:09:56,933
<b>and Honduras' own government calling</b>

284
01:09:56,933 --> 01:09:58,533
<b>these islands British territory.</b>

285
01:09:59,166 --> 01:10:01,066
<b>The same judges hearing this case will</b>

286
01:10:01,066 --> 01:10:02,966
<b>eventually rule on Guatemala's claim to</b>

287
01:10:02,966 --> 01:10:04,133
<b>the Belizean mainland.</b>

288
01:10:04,566 --> 01:10:06,566
<b>And the reasoning they develop here about</b>

289
01:10:06,566 --> 01:10:07,899
<b>Spanish colonial succession,</b>

290
01:10:08,399 --> 01:10:09,733
<b>about what counts as effective</b>

291
01:10:09,733 --> 01:10:11,600
<b>administration, carries</b>

292
01:10:11,600 --> 01:10:13,033
<b>straight into that case.</b>

293
01:10:13,699 --> 01:10:15,899
<b>The ICJ just allowed the country to sit</b>

294
01:10:15,899 --> 01:10:16,633
<b>in someone else's</b>

295
01:10:16,633 --> 01:10:18,699
<b>courtroom, not as a party,</b>

296
01:10:18,933 --> 01:10:21,600
<b>not bound by the ruling, purely to stop</b>

297
01:10:21,600 --> 01:10:22,666
<b>the court from building a</b>

298
01:10:22,666 --> 01:10:24,133
<b>legal record it can't undo.</b>

299
01:10:25,033 --> 01:10:26,833
<b>That's only the fourth time in 80 years</b>

300
01:10:26,833 --> 01:10:28,133
<b>the court has done this.</b>

301
01:10:28,666 --> 01:10:31,366
<b>Fishermen from Punta Gorda, 75 kilometers</b>

302
01:10:31,366 --> 01:10:32,666
<b>from Sapodilla Cayes,</b>

303
01:10:33,199 --> 01:10:34,733
<b>still depend on these waters.</b>

304
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:37,233
<b>Three governments are now fighting over</b>

305
01:10:37,233 --> 01:10:38,133
<b>where they can fish.</b>

306
01:10:39,033 --> 01:10:40,633
<b>None of these governments ask them.</b>

307
01:10:41,133 --> 01:10:43,399
<b>The main case, whether Guatemala gets</b>

308
01:10:43,399 --> 01:10:46,233
<b>half of Belize is expected in 2027.</b>

309
01:10:47,066 --> 01:10:48,333
<b>I'll cover it when it drops.</b>

310
01:10:49,233 --> 01:10:50,600
<b>Please subscribe if you</b>

311
01:10:50,600 --> 01:10:51,699
<b>want to follow this case.</b>

